      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T14:23:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, that doesn\u0027t seem right... prashkre, it seems like the caller messed up if they specified an ldap_attr_name that isn\u0027t valid in attribute_mapping, right? Is there a valid case where the caller should be allowed to specify an ldap_attr_name that doesn\u0027t exist in attribute_mapping? If not, we should raise an exception and make them fix that. Maybe just remove the \"if not attr\" check entirely?\n\nIf there is a valid case for ldap_attr_name not existing in attribute_mapping, we need more information about what that is in order to decide what the best way to handle it is.",
      "parentUuid": "ff346bd7_8224345f",
