        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T20:06:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I imagine that if you do nothing (i.e., just remove the \"if not attr\" block) it will blow up a couple lines lower and a) the admin should see a nice stack trace in the logs and b) an API caller would get an HTTP 500. And that sounds about right to me.",
