    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df3967d1_ba9df567",
        "filename": "keystone/identity/backends/ldap/common.py",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1396,
      "author": {
        "id": 24005
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T19:55:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lets consider the ldap configuration as shown in [1]\n\none example of obj is (u\u0027uid\u003dfakeUid,c\u003dfake,ou\u003dfakedomain,o\u003dfakeorg\u0027, {\u0027identity\u0027: [u\u0027fakename\u0027], \u0027mail\u0027: [u\u0027fake@fakeorg.org\u0027], \u0027uid\u0027: [u\u0027fakeUid\u0027]}) where ldap_result is a list of type \u003ctuple\u003e,\n\nSince _filter_ldap_result_by_attr() method is being called with ldap_attr_name \u003d \"name\", from [0] and [1] attr is being set with value \"identity\" from self.attribute_mapping\n\n\nSo,\nobj[1].get(attr) is [u\u0027fakename\u0027], which is a list and in if conditional statement, it checks for list is empty or None.\n\nobj[1].get(attr)[0] is fakename, which is a string and in if conditional statement, it checks for empty string or None.\n\n\n[0] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/identity/backends/ldap/common.py#L1155\nhttps://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/identity/backends/ldap/core.py#L243\n\n[1]\n[ldap]\nurl \u003d ldap://9.9.9.9\nuser_name_attribute \u003d identity\nuser_id_attribute \u003d uid\nuser_mail_attribute \u003d mail",
      "parentUuid": "ff346bd7_22fc68b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1396,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 1396,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "c7b536d40fc7ee30ce54011fe0ff5a846eff3300",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
